  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to UNICEF for Life-saving Treatment for Children with Severe Acute Malnutrition in Lao PDR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention aims to improve survival and recovery outcomes for 3,500 children under five suffering from Severe Acute Malnutrition in Laos through uninterrupted supply of ready to use supplements (RUTF), a life saving treatment. FCDO contribution will fill a critical funding gap in the ongoing programme which threatens the continuity of the national RUTF supply pipeline, serving as a bridge financing mechanism while UNICEF and the Government pursue longer-term financing solutions. The intervention builds upon UNICEF&apos;s broader nutrition programme which includes the IMAM system established with the Ministry of Health. This investment directly complements UNICEF&apos;s existing programming in 11 provinces supported by CNF programmatic funding.</narrative>
  </description>
